<!-- Tagalog. Shown when the app language is Tagalog (Settings > Wika ng app), or when the phone
     itself is set to Filipino: Android treats "tl" and "fil" as the same language, and its own
     Filipino translations live in values-tl too.

     The words follow the way Android and Google apps are translated into Filipino: plain Tagalog,
     with the technical words people already say in English kept in English (channel, signal,
     scan, tuner, dongle, antenna, frequency, caption, record, data broadcast). opendtv/TRANSLATING.md
     has the word list and the rules, for a new screen or a fix.

     A string missing here falls back to the English one, so a new screen never breaks; it just
     shows in English until its Tagalog is added. -->
